N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match]/2-3: P<int, char, char> matches the
constrained partial specialization `P<A, Args...>' with Args = {char, char}.
The front end selected the primary template (n == 0, bin53): a
constrained specialization is re-matched in elaborate_class_template, whose
matcher let a trailing pack absorb a longer argument list only for two or
more packs.  A single pack now does too.  The same shape as libstdc++'s
views::__adaptor::_Partial.  g++
13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
